[[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Unscrew the screws.</p><p>2. Remove the cushion (2a) of the seat by disconnecting it from\nthe rear check rods (2b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2019422.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Make sure that the cushion\n is not damaged.</p><p>Place the seat and secure it to the rear\ncheck rods.</p><p>Pull out the rear seat belts.</p><p>Screw the screws and tighten them to the\ngiven torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>REAR SEAT CUSHION</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>2.2 - 2.6</p></td></tr></table></div>"]]